User: Write a MATLAB program that performs a principal component analysis (PCA) on a dataset with at least five variables. The program should include data input and output, calculation of the covariance matrix, extraction of the eigenvectors and eigenvalues, selection of the principal components, and visualization of the results using a scatter plot or a biplot. The program should be well-documented, well-organized, and efficient, and it should handle missing values and outliers appropriately. Test the program on a small example dataset before applying it to larger and more complex datasets.
Assistant: % Principal Component Analysis (PCA) in MATLAB
% This program performs PCA on a dataset with at least 5 variables
% The program includes data input and output, calculation of covariance matrix, 
% extraction of eigenvectors and eigenvalues, selection of principal components, 
% visualization of results using scatter plot or biplot

%% Step 1: Data Input and Output
% Input format: comma-separated values (CSV) file or MATLAB data file (MAT)
% Output format: save figures and data tables as JPEG or PNG files

% Import dataset
data = readtable('sample_data.csv');

% Display data and summary statistics
disp(data)
summary(data)

%% Step 2: Data Preprocessing
% Missing values treatment: replace with mean or median, or delete 
% Outlier detection and treatment: remove or replace with mean or median

% Treat missing values
data = fillmissing(data,'movmedian',3);

% Detect and treat outliers
zScores = zscore(data);
isOutlier = abs(zScores)>3;
data(isOutlier) = NaN;
data = fillmissing(data,'nearest');

% Display updated data
disp(data)
summary(data)

%% Step 3: Covariance Matrix Calculation
% Calculate covariance matrix
covMatrix = cov(data);

% Display covariance matrix
disp('Covariance Matrix:');
disp(covMatrix);

%% Step 4: Extraction of Eigenvectors and Eigenvalues
% Calculate eigenvectors and eigenvalues 
[coeff,score,latent] = pca(data);

% Display eigenvectors and eigenvalues
disp('Eigenvectors:');
disp(coeff);
disp('Eigenvalues:');
disp(latent);

% Extract first two principal components
PC1 = score(:,1);
PC2 = score(:,2);

%% Step 5: Visualization of Results
% Visualize results using scatter plot or biplot
% Scatter plot
figure;
scatter(PC1,PC2);
title('PCA Scatter Plot')
xlabel('Principal Component 1');
ylabel('Principal Component 2');

% Biplots
figure;
biplot(coeff(:,1:2),'Scores',score(:,1:2),'VarLabels',{'Var1','Var2','Var3','Var4','Var5'});
title('PCA Biplots') 
xlabel('Principal Component 1');
ylabel('Principal Component 2');

%% Step 6: Data Export
% Export data tables and figures as JPEG or PNG files

% Export data
writetable(data,'sample_data_processed.csv');

% Export figures
savefig('PCA_scatter_plot.fig');
saveas(gcf,'PCA_scatter_plot.jpg');

savefig('PCA_biplots.fig');
saveas(gcf,'PCA_biplots.jpg'); 
disp('Program executed successfully!');
